  model notes ```
# Physiologically based pharmacokinetic/pharmacodynamic (PBPK/PD) model apixaban
(body model)

Whole-body physiologically based pharmacokinetic/pharmacodynamic (PBPK/PD)model of
apixaban, built with the PBPK library `pkpdsim.pbpk`: thedissolution of the tablet and the incomplete
absorption of apixaban in theintestine, its efflux into the intestinal lumen (P-gp,
BCRP), thedistribution into the tissues, the metabolism by CYP3A4 in the liver toO-demethyl
apixaban (M2), hydroxy apixaban (M7) and O-demethyl apixabansulfate (M1), the renal
excretion of apixaban, M1 and M7 and the biliaryexcretion of the metabolites, and
the anticoagulant effects (anti-factor Xaactivity, INR, PT, mPT, aPTT) of the total
apixaban concentration of theplasma, with the effects of impaired renal and hepatic
function, of thebody weight and of the interactions of CYP3A4 and P-gp.

The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.

