- Carlsson M, Andersson R, Bloch KM, Steding-Ehrenborg K, Mosén H, Stahlberg F, Ekmehag B, Arheden H. Cardiac output and cardiac index measured with cardiovascular magnetic resonance in healthy subjects, elite athletes and patients with congestive heart failure. J Cardiovasc Magn Reson 14(1):51, 2012. doi:10.1186/1532-429X-14-51
```
  fage_Qrest notes ```
The share of the cardiac output of the organs besides the brain relative to the adults,
`(1 - fQbr*fage_Qbr * fsex_Qbr)/(1 - fQbr)`.

`fage_Qrest = (1 dimensionless - 0.13040643338404695 dimensionless * fage_Qbr * fsex_Qbr) / 0.8695935666159531 dimensionless` 

Sources:

- Chiron C, Raynaud C, Maziere B, Zilbovicius M, Laflamme L, Masure MC, Dulac O, Bourguignon M, Syrota A. Changes in regional cerebral blood flow during brain maturation in children and adolescents. J Nucl Med 33(5):696-703, 1992. PMID 1569478.
- Zoli M, Magalotti D, Bianchi G, Gueli C, Orlandini C, Grimaldi M, Marchesini G. Total and functional hepatic blood flow decrease in parallel with ageing. Age Ageing 28(1):29-33, 1999. doi:10.1093/ageing/28.1.29
- Davies DF, Shock NW. Age changes in glomerular filtration rate, effective renal plasma flow, and tubular excretory capacity in adult males. J Clin Invest 29(5):496-507, 1950. doi:10.1172/JCI102286
- Carlsson M, Andersson R, Bloch KM, Steding-Ehrenborg K, Mosén H, Stahlberg F, Ekmehag B, Arheden H. Cardiac output and cardiac index measured with cardiovascular magnetic resonance in healthy subjects, elite athletes and patients with congestive heart failure. J Cardiovasc Magn Reson 14(1):51, 2012. doi:10.1186/1532-429X-14-51
```
  fsex_Qbr notes ```
The factor of the sex on the brain fraction of the cardiac output of the female individual
of 35 years relative to a man of the same body weight and height (`pkpdsim.pbpk.sex_differences`): The cerebral
blood flow per mass of young women is higher than of men: PET 15O-water +17 % at
20 years and +2 % at 65 years (Aanerud 2017, n = 58, cortical grey matter, Table
1), pCASL +16.5 % (Alisch 2021, n = 80), Xe-133 +11 % at all ages (Rodriguez 1988),
and the total cerebral blood flow by phase-contrast MRI is higher despite a smaller
brain (Xing 2017, 21-45 years, 724 +- 112 women and 551 +- 111 ml/min men, 21.3 and
14.8 % of the cardiac output); ICRP 89 gives both sexes 12 % of the cardiac output
and the same perfusion per mass. The factor on the brain fraction of the cardiac
output of the women (the other fractions share the rest in their proportions) gives
the perfusion per mass of the female reference individual 1.17 times the male at
18-45 years and 1.02 from 65 years (Aanerud 2017 at 65 years, Smith 2019 -4 % with
the hematocrit of each subject, Alisch 2021 70-79 years +3 %), with the factor of
the cardiac output: 1.17/0.931 = 1.257 and 1.02/0.931 = 1.096 (0.931 the perfusion
ratio of the references with the cardiac output factor alone); 1 until 12 years (no
difference before puberty, Satterthwaite 2014, n = 922, 8-22 years, the divergence
at mid-puberty, and Wu 2016), the rise over puberty and the fall from 45 to 65 years
(the faster decline of the women, Aanerud 2017 -3.8 against -1.0 % per decade) linear,
a choice.

Sources:

- Aanerud J, Borghammer P, Rodell A, Jónsdottir KY, Gjedde A. Sex differences of human cortical blood flow and energy metabolism. J Cereb Blood Flow Metab 37(7):2433-2440, 2017. doi:10.1177/0271678X16668536
- Alisch JSR, Khattar N, Kim RW, Cortina LE, Rejimon AC, Qian W, Ferrucci L, Resnick SM, Spencer RG, Bouhrara M. Sex and age-related differences in cerebral blood flow investigated using pseudo-continuous arterial spin labeling magnetic resonance imaging. Aging (Albany NY) 13(4):4911-4925, 2021. doi:10.18632/aging.202673
- Rodriguez G, Warkentin S, Risberg J, Rosadini G. Sex differences in regional cerebral blood flow. J Cereb Blood Flow Metab 8(6):783-789, 1988. doi:10.1038/jcbfm.1988.133
- Xing CY, Tarumi T, Liu J, Zhang Y, Turner M, Riley J, Tinajero CD, Yuan LJ, Zhang R. Distribution of cardiac output to the brain across the adult lifespan. J Cereb Blood Flow Metab 37(8):2848-2856, 2017. doi:10.1177/0271678X16676826
- Satterthwaite TD, Shinohara RT, Wolf DH, Hopson RD, Elliott MA, Vandekar SN, Ruparel K, Calkins ME, Roalf DR, Gennatas ED, Jackson C, Erus G, Prabhakaran K, Davatzikos C, Detre JA, Hakonarson H, Gur RC, Gur RE. Impact of puberty on the evolution of cerebral perfusion during adolescence. Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A 111(23):8643-8648, 2014. doi:10.1073/pnas.1400178111
- Smith LA, Melbourne A, Owen D, Cardoso MJ, Sudre CH, Tillin T, Sokolska M, Atkinson D, Chaturvedi N, Ourselin S, Hughes AD, Barkhof F, Jäger HR. Cortical cerebral blood flow in ageing: effects of haematocrit, sex, ethnicity and diabetes. Eur Radiol 29(10):5549-5558, 2019. doi:10.1007/s00330-019-06096-w
```
  fage_Qother notes ```
The factor which closes the sum of the fractions: the share of the organs besides
the brain, the liver group and the kidney, relative to the adults.

`fage_Qother = (1 dimensionless - 0.13040643338404695 dimensionless - 0.07063681808302542 dimensionless * fage_Qli - 0.05433601391001956 dimensionless * fage_Qli - 0.010867202782003912 dimensionless * fage_Qli - 0.11953923060204304 dimensionless * fage_Qli - 0.03260160834601174 dimensionless * fage_Qli - 0.010867202782003912 dimensionless * fage_Qli - 0.18474244729406653 dimensionless * fage_Qki) / 0.3860030428167789 dimensionless` 

Sources:

- Chiron C, Raynaud C, Maziere B, Zilbovicius M, Laflamme L, Masure MC, Dulac O, Bourguignon M, Syrota A. Changes in regional cerebral blood flow during brain maturation in children and adolescents. J Nucl Med 33(5):696-703, 1992. PMID 1569478.
- Zoli M, Magalotti D, Bianchi G, Gueli C, Orlandini C, Grimaldi M, Marchesini G. Total and functional hepatic blood flow decrease in parallel with ageing. Age Ageing 28(1):29-33, 1999. doi:10.1093/ageing/28.1.29
- Davies DF, Shock NW. Age changes in glomerular filtration rate, effective renal plasma flow, and tubular excretory capacity in adult males. J Clin Invest 29(5):496-507, 1950. doi:10.1172/JCI102286
- Carlsson M, Andersson R, Bloch KM, Steding-Ehrenborg K, Mosén H, Stahlberg F, Ekmehag B, Arheden H. Cardiac output and cardiac index measured with cardiovascular magnetic resonance in healthy subjects, elite athletes and patients with congestive heart failure. J Cardiovasc Magn Reson 14(1):51, 2012. doi:10.1186/1532-429X-14-51
```
