```
  LI__kps_api notes ```
Passive exchange per litre of organ, given instead of the share of the whole-body
exchange; the organ has `kps_api * Vli`.

Fast exchange (not fitted), the role of the instant import and export of apixaban
(`1000/min * Vli`) of the hand-written model: 100 l/min of the unbound substance for the whole
liver of the reference individual, per litre of liver 100 l/min / 2.33 l = 42.9 1/min.
It does not limit the hepatic clearance of apixaban: the total clearance after an
iv dose is 52.65 ml/min with it, 52.69 ml/min with 100 times the exchange (hepatic
23.2 ml/min, 0.1 %); the exchange of the unbound M1 and M7 is 1150 and 320 times
their biliary clearance of the unbound metabolite (0.087 and 0.31 l/min).
```
  LI__PS_api notes ```
Passive exchange between plasma and tissue: the exchange per litre of organ times
the organ volume, so it follows the organ of the individual. The functional share
`f_functional` of the tissue of the liver.

`PS_api = kps_api * Vli * f_functional`
```
  LI__Cu_ti_api notes ```
Unbound concentration of the tissue; an observer.

`Cu_ti_api = fu_api / Kp_api * Cti_api`
```
  LI__f_water_int notes ```
water fraction of the interstitial fluid; httk 2.7.4 sets it to the water fraction
of plasma (R/predict_partitioning_schmitt.R: FWint = FWpl), 1 - 0.06951; read in
httk (MIT), Schmitt 2008 itself not read

Source:

- Pearce RG, Setzer RW, Strope CL, Wambaugh JF, Sipes NS. httk: R package for high-throughput toxicokinetics. J Stat Softw 79(4):1-26, 2017. R package httk version 2.7.4 (CRAN, 2025-12-08), MIT license, copyright 2025 John Wambaugh; the data set mecdt of HTTK-Pop (Ring 2017) holds the preprocessed NHANES 2013-2018 respondents. doi:10.18637/jss.v079.i04
```
  LI__f_water_pls notes ```
water fraction of plasma; httk 2.7.4 R/predict_partitioning_schmitt.R: FWpl = 1 -
Fprotein.plasma, with the plasma protein volume fraction 0.06951 of the human column
of physiology.data (&apos;Plasma Protein Volume Fraction&apos;); read in httk (MIT),
Schmitt 2008 itself not read

Source:

- Pearce RG, Setzer RW, Strope CL, Wambaugh JF, Sipes NS. httk: R package for high-throughput toxicokinetics. J Stat Softw 79(4):1-26, 2017. R package httk version 2.7.4 (CRAN, 2025-12-08), MIT license, copyright 2025 John Wambaugh; the data set mecdt of HTTK-Pop (Ring 2017) holds the preprocessed NHANES 2013-2018 respondents. doi:10.18637/jss.v079.i04
```
  LI__r_protein_int_pls notes ```
protein of the interstitial fluid relative to plasma; httk 2.7.4 R/predict_partitioning_schmitt.R:
FPint = 0.37 \* Fprotein.plasma, the ratio FPint/Fprotein.plasma of Kint, Schmitt
2008 equation 4 as httk implements it; read in httk (MIT), Schmitt 2008 itself not
read

Source:

- Pearce RG, Setzer RW, Strope CL, Wambaugh JF, Sipes NS. httk: R package for high-throughput toxicokinetics. J Stat Softw 79(4):1-26, 2017. R package httk version 2.7.4 (CRAN, 2025-12-08), MIT license, copyright 2025 John Wambaugh; the data set mecdt of HTTK-Pop (Ring 2017) holds the preprocessed NHANES 2013-2018 respondents. doi:10.18637/jss.v079.i04
```
  LI__K_int_pls_api_m1 notes ```
Interstitial to plasma coefficient (Schmitt 2008): the water of the interstitium
and the plasma proteins of the interstitial fluid.

`K_int_pls_api_m1 = (f_water_int + r_protein_int_pls * (1 dimensionless / fu_api_m1 - f_water_pls)) * fu_api_m1`
```
  LI__K_cell_pls_api_m1 notes ```
Intracellular to plasma coefficient such that interstitium and cells together have
the whole-tissue Kp, `(f_int*K_int_pls + f_cell*K_cell_pls)/(f_int + f_cell) = Kp`. The Kp must exceed the interstitial share `f_int*K_int_pls/(f_int + f_cell)` (the lower
bound of a fitted Kp); below it the coefficient is floored at 1e-06.

`K_cell_pls_api_m1 = piecewise((Kp_api_m1 * (f_int_li + (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li)) - f_int_li * K_int_pls_api_m1) / (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li), (Kp_api_m1 * (f_int_li + (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li)) - f_int_li * K_int_pls_api_m1) / (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li) > 1e-06 dimensionless, 1e-06 dimensionless)`
```
  LI__k_vas notes ```
exchange between plasma and interstitium per organ volume, PS_vas = k_vas \* V; chosen
so that the equilibration of the interstitium (time constant f_int \* K_int_pls /
(k_vas \* fu), below 0.05 min in every organ for fu >= 0.005) is fast against
the passage of the blood through an organ (f_vas \* V / Q, about 0.1 to 1 min), i.e.
the endothelium does not limit the exchange of small molecules

Source:

- Choice of a library of pkpdsim (PBPK or machine perfusion), not a value of the literature; the notes of the value give the reasoning.
```
  LI__PS_vas notes ```
Exchange between plasma and interstitium across the endothelium.

`PS_vas = k_vas * Vli`
```
  LI__kps_api_m1 notes ```
Passive exchange per litre of organ, given instead of the share of the whole-body
exchange; the organ has `kps_api_m1 * Vli`.

Fast exchange (not fitted), the role of the instant import and export of O-demethyl
apixaban sulfate (M1) (`1000/min * Vli`) of the hand-written model: 100 l/min of the unbound substance
for the whole liver of the reference individual, per litre of liver 100 l/min / 2.33
l = 42.9 1/min. It does not limit the hepatic clearance of apixaban: the total clearance
after an iv dose is 52.65 ml/min with it, 52.69 ml/min with 100 times the exchange
(hepatic 23.2 ml/min, 0.1 %); the exchange of the unbound M1 and M7 is 1150 and 320
times their biliary clearance of the unbound metabolite (0.087 and 0.31 l/min).
```
  LI__PS_api_m1 notes ```
Passive exchange between plasma and tissue: the exchange per litre of organ times
the organ volume, so it follows the organ of the individual. The functional share
`f_functional` of the tissue of the liver.

`PS_api_m1 = kps_api_m1 * Vli * f_functional`
```
  LI__Cu_is_api_m1 notes ```
Unbound concentration of the interstitium; an observer.

`Cu_is_api_m1 = fu_api_m1 / K_int_pls_api_m1 * Cis_api_m1`
```
  LI__Cu_ic_api_m1 notes ```
Unbound concentration of the intracellular space; an observer.

`Cu_ic_api_m1 = fu_api_m1 / K_cell_pls_api_m1 * Cic_api_m1`
```
  LI__K_int_pls_api_m2 notes ```
Interstitial to plasma coefficient (Schmitt 2008): the water of the interstitium
and the plasma proteins of the interstitial fluid.

`K_int_pls_api_m2 = (f_water_int + r_protein_int_pls * (1 dimensionless / fu_api_m2 - f_water_pls)) * fu_api_m2`
```
  LI__K_cell_pls_api_m2 notes ```
The substance does not distribute into the tissue of the organ: without a Kp the
cells bind it as the interstitial fluid.

`K_cell_pls_api_m2 = K_int_pls_api_m2`
```
  LI__PS_api_m2 notes ```
No passive exchange: the substance does not distribute into the tissue of the organ,
it enters the cells by its transporters only.
```
  LI__Cu_is_api_m2 notes ```
Unbound concentration of the interstitium; an observer.

`Cu_is_api_m2 = fu_api_m2 / K_int_pls_api_m2 * Cis_api_m2`
```
  LI__Cu_ic_api_m2 notes ```
Unbound concentration of the intracellular space; an observer.

`Cu_ic_api_m2 = fu_api_m2 / K_cell_pls_api_m2 * Cic_api_m2`
```
  LI__K_int_pls_api_m7 notes ```
Interstitial to plasma coefficient (Schmitt 2008): the water of the interstitium
and the plasma proteins of the interstitial fluid.

`K_int_pls_api_m7 = (f_water_int + r_protein_int_pls * (1 dimensionless / fu_api_m7 - f_water_pls)) * fu_api_m7`
```
  LI__K_cell_pls_api_m7 notes ```
Intracellular to plasma coefficient such that interstitium and cells together have
the whole-tissue Kp, `(f_int*K_int_pls + f_cell*K_cell_pls)/(f_int + f_cell) = Kp`. The Kp must exceed the interstitial share `f_int*K_int_pls/(f_int + f_cell)` (the lower
bound of a fitted Kp); below it the coefficient is floored at 1e-06.

`K_cell_pls_api_m7 = piecewise((Kp_api_m7 * (f_int_li + (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li)) - f_int_li * K_int_pls_api_m7) / (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li), (Kp_api_m7 * (f_int_li + (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li)) - f_int_li * K_int_pls_api_m7) / (1 dimensionless - f_vas_li - f_int_li) > 1e-06 dimensionless, 1e-06 dimensionless)`
```
  LI__kps_api_m7 notes ```
Passive exchange per litre of organ, given instead of the share of the whole-body
exchange; the organ has `kps_api_m7 * Vli`.

Fast exchange (not fitted), the role of the instant import and export of hydroxy
apixaban (M7) (`1000/min * Vli`) of the hand-written model: 100 l/min of the unbound substance
for the whole liver of the reference individual, per litre of liver 100 l/min / 2.33
l = 42.9 1/min. It does not limit the hepatic clearance of apixaban: the total clearance
after an iv dose is 52.65 ml/min with it, 52.69 ml/min with 100 times the exchange
(hepatic 23.2 ml/min, 0.1 %); the exchange of the unbound M1 and M7 is 1150 and 320
times their biliary clearance of the unbound metabolite (0.087 and 0.31 l/min).
```
  LI__PS_api_m7 notes ```
Passive exchange between plasma and tissue: the exchange per litre of organ times
the organ volume, so it follows the organ of the individual. The functional share
`f_functional` of the tissue of the liver.

`PS_api_m7 = kps_api_m7 * Vli * f_functional`
```
  LI__Cu_is_api_m7 notes ```
Unbound concentration of the interstitium; an observer.

`Cu_is_api_m7 = fu_api_m7 / K_int_pls_api_m7 * Cis_api_m7`
```
  LI__Cu_ic_api_m7 notes ```
Unbound concentration of the intracellular space; an observer.

`Cu_ic_api_m7 = fu_api_m7 / K_cell_pls_api_m7 * Cic_api_m7`
```
  LI__f_cyp3a4 notes ```
Base activity of CYP3A4 in the organ relative to normal (1.0), set by genotype, impairment
and the experiments; it multiplies the rates of its processes. Inhibition and induction
act on top of it (the turnover state and the inhibitor terms of the rates).
```
  LI__f_sult1a1 notes ```
Base activity of SULT1A1 in the organ relative to normal (1.0), set by genotype,
impairment and the experiments; it multiplies the rates of its processes. Inhibition
and induction act on top of it (the turnover state and the inhibitor terms of the
rates).
```
  LI__API2M_k notes ```
Clearance per litre of organ on the unbound concentration; the organ has `API2M_k * Vli`.

The metabolism of the unbound apixaban by CYP3A4/5 per litre of liver. The fraction
0.78 into M2 (O-demethylation, M2 and its products M1, M10, M13), the rest into M7
(hydroxylation): about 17-18 % vs 5 % of the dose in the urine and feces (Raghavan2009,
Table 4).

Fitted value.
```
  LI__M22M1_k notes ```
Clearance per litre of organ on the unbound concentration; the organ has `M22M1_k * Vli`.

The sulfation of M2 into M1 (SULT1A1) per litre of liver. M2 sits in the liver cells
of the library (`LI__Vic`), it has no passive exchange; its fate is the sulfation into M1
and the biliary excretion.

Fitted value.
```
  LI__M1EXBI_k notes ```
Clearance per litre of organ on the unbound concentration; the organ has `M1EXBI_k * Vli`.

The excretion of the unbound M1 into the bile per litre of liver (the library reads
the unbound concentration of the cell), informed by the fecal metabolites (Raghavan2009).

Fitted value.
```
  LI__M2EXBI_k notes ```
Clearance per litre of organ on the unbound concentration; the organ has `M2EXBI_k * Vli`.

Not fitted, the rate of the biliary excretion of M1 per unbound concentration and
litre of liver (`LI__M1EXBI_k` 0.03695 1/min of a fit with all 15 parameters, cost 105.215, whose
record is not kept): the profile likelihood of `LI__M2EXBI_k` in that fit was open upwards (95
% CI 0.0111 1/min to its upper bound 0.676), the rate of M1, the sulfate of M2, lies
within it (that of M7, 0.132 1/min, as well); the fit was repeated with this value
(PK_20261026_144013__f7a78). M2 sits in the liver cells of the library (`LI__Vic`), it has
no passive exchange; its fate is the sulfation into M1 and the biliary excretion.
```
  LI__M7EXBI_k notes ```
Clearance per litre of organ on the unbound concentration; the organ has `M7EXBI_k * Vli`.

The excretion of the unbound M7 into the bile per litre of liver (the library reads
the unbound concentration of the cell), informed by the fecal metabolites (Raghavan2009).

Fitted value.
```
  Cout_ki_api notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api = Cpl_api`
```
  KI__PS_api notes ```
Passive exchange between plasma and tissue: the share of the whole-body exchange
`ftissue` by the tissue volume of the organ relative to the reference tissue volume. ftissue
multiplies `fu*(Cpl - Cti/Kp)` (the unbound plasma concentration and the tissue concentration as plasma
equivalent), so its fitted values differ from those of the hand-written models, where
it multiplied the total concentrations.

`PS_api = ftissue_api * Vki * (1 dimensionless - f_vas_ki) / Vti_total_ref_api`
```
  KI__Cu_ti_api notes ```
Unbound concentration of the tissue; an observer.

`Cu_ti_api = fu_api / Kp_api * Cti_api`
```
  Cout_ki_api_m1 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m1 = Cpl_api_m1`
```
  Cout_ki_api_m2 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m2 = Cpl_api_m2`
```
  Cout_ki_api_m7 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m7 = Cpl_api_m7`
```
  Rurine_api notes ```
The rate of the urinary excretion: the sum of the fluxes of the kidney into the urine.

`Rurine_api = J_gfr_api`
```
  Rurine_api_m1 notes ```
The rate of the urinary excretion: the sum of the fluxes of the kidney into the urine.

`Rurine_api_m1 = J_gfr_api_m1`
```
  Rurine_api_m7 notes ```
The rate of the urinary excretion: the sum of the fluxes of the kidney into the urine.

`Rurine_api_m7 = J_gfr_api_m7`
```
  Cout_st_api notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api = Cpl_api`
```
  ST__PS_api notes ```
Passive exchange between plasma and tissue: the share of the whole-body exchange
`ftissue` by the tissue volume of the organ relative to the reference tissue volume. ftissue
multiplies `fu*(Cpl - Cti/Kp)` (the unbound plasma concentration and the tissue concentration as plasma
equivalent), so its fitted values differ from those of the hand-written models, where
it multiplied the total concentrations.

`PS_api = ftissue_api * Vst * (1 dimensionless - f_vas_st) / Vti_total_ref_api`
```
  ST__Cu_ti_api notes ```
Unbound concentration of the tissue; an observer.

`Cu_ti_api = fu_api / Kp_api * Cti_api`
```
  Cout_st_api_m1 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m1 = Cpl_api_m1`
```
  Cout_st_api_m2 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m2 = Cpl_api_m2`
```
  Cout_st_api_m7 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m7 = Cpl_api_m7`
```
  GU__Vmu_total notes ```
Volume of the mucosa of all segments.

`Vmu_total = Vmu_du + Vmu_jej1 + Vmu_jej2 + Vmu_ile1 + Vmu_ile2 + Vmu_cae + Vmu_asc + Vmu_tra + Vmu_des + Vmu_sig + Vmu_rec`
```
  GU__T_st notes ```
Mean transit time of the lumen segment (fasted), the transit into the next segment
is `V*C/T`.

Table 6, fasted half-emptying time 15.8 min (300 ml water, range 11.5-17.0 min) as
mean residence time of a first order emptying, 15.8 min / ln 2

Source:

- Mudie DM, Amidon GL, Amidon GE. Physiological parameters for oral delivery and in vitro testing. Mol Pharm 7(5):1388-1405, 2010. doi:10.1021/mp100149j
```
  GU__T_du notes ```
Mean transit time of the lumen segment (fasted), the transit into the next segment
is `V*C/T`.

Table 6, small intestinal transit time fasted 192 min (coated pellets, range 90-324
min), by the length share 21/282 of the duodenum (Table 4)

Source:

- Mudie DM, Amidon GL, Amidon GE. Physiological parameters for oral delivery and in vitro testing. Mol Pharm 7(5):1388-1405, 2010. doi:10.1021/mp100149j
```
