  GU__f_area_cae notes ```
Mucosal surface per lumen volume relative to the small intestine: the absorption
of the segment is `ka*f_area`.

mucosal surface per lumen volume relative to the small intestine:
(A_LI/A_SI)*(L_SI/L_LI)*(d_SI/d_LI)^2 = (2/30)*2*(2.5/4.8)^2 with the mucosal surfaces
2 m2 (large intestine) and 30 m2 (small intestine, of 32 m2 in total), the small
intestine two thirds of the oroanal length and the inner diameters 2.5 and 4.8 cm;
the lumen a cylinder of the inner diameter; permeability differences are not included

Source:

- Helander HF, Fändriks L. Surface area of the digestive tract - revisited. Scand J Gastroenterol 49(6):681-689, 2014. doi:10.3109/00365521.2014.898326
```
