  GU__kdis_api notes ```
Dissolution rate of the undissolved drug in every segment.

`kdis_api = Ka_dis_api / 60 min_per_hr * D50_dis_api / (D50_dis_api + (PODOSE_api + Mr_api * (Asolid_du_api + Asolid_jej1_api + Asolid_jej2_api + Asolid_ile1_api + Asolid_ile2_api + Asolid_cae_api + Asolid_asc_api + Asolid_tra_api + Asolid_des_api + Asolid_sig_api + Asolid_rec_api)))`
```
  Cout_si_api_m1 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m1 = Cpl_api_m1`
```
  Cout_si_api_m2 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m2 = Cpl_api_m2`
```
  Cout_si_api_m7 notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api_m7 = Cpl_api_m7`
```
  GU__f_abcb1 notes ```
Base activity of ABCB1 in the organ relative to normal (1.0), set by genotype, impairment
and the experiments; it multiplies the rates of its processes. Inhibition and induction
act on top of it (the turnover state and the inhibitor terms of the rates).
```
  GU__w_uniform_du notes ```
Share of a process of the protein in the mucosa of the segment, by mucosa volume
over the segments of the small intestine (the protein has no expression data)

`w_uniform_du = Vmu_du / (Vmu_du + Vmu_jej1 + Vmu_jej2 + Vmu_ile1 + Vmu_ile2)`
```
  GU__APISEC_k notes ```
Clearance per litre of organ on the unbound concentration; the organ has `APISEC_k * Vsi`.

The efflux of the unbound apixaban from the enterocytes into the lumen (P-gp, BCRP
lumped, `f_abcb1`), per litre of small intestine. Apixaban is eliminated unchanged into
the gut (Frost2021, Wang2014: activated charcoal lowers the AUC); the efflux acts
on the absorbed apixaban as well.

Fitted value.
```
  GU__w_uniform_jej1 notes ```
Share of a process of the protein in the mucosa of the segment, by mucosa volume
over the segments of the small intestine (the protein has no expression data)

`w_uniform_jej1 = Vmu_jej1 / (Vmu_du + Vmu_jej1 + Vmu_jej2 + Vmu_ile1 + Vmu_ile2)`
```
  GU__w_uniform_jej2 notes ```
Share of a process of the protein in the mucosa of the segment, by mucosa volume
over the segments of the small intestine (the protein has no expression data)

`w_uniform_jej2 = Vmu_jej2 / (Vmu_du + Vmu_jej1 + Vmu_jej2 + Vmu_ile1 + Vmu_ile2)`
```
  GU__w_uniform_ile1 notes ```
Share of a process of the protein in the mucosa of the segment, by mucosa volume
over the segments of the small intestine (the protein has no expression data)

`w_uniform_ile1 = Vmu_ile1 / (Vmu_du + Vmu_jej1 + Vmu_jej2 + Vmu_ile1 + Vmu_ile2)`
```
  GU__w_uniform_ile2 notes ```
Share of a process of the protein in the mucosa of the segment, by mucosa volume
over the segments of the small intestine (the protein has no expression data)

`w_uniform_ile2 = Vmu_ile2 / (Vmu_du + Vmu_jej1 + Vmu_jej2 + Vmu_ile1 + Vmu_ile2)`
```
  T_st_eff notes ```
The transit time of the stomach of the prandial state and the impairment, which its
transit reads: `T_st` fasted, `T_st_fed` fed (`FED = 1`; times the factor of the sex), times the factor
of the gastric emptying of chronic kidney disease; an output of the intestine, an
id of the top model.

`T_st_eff = (T_st + FED * (T_st_fed * fsex_t_stomach_fed - T_st)) * fimp_t_stomach`
```
  Rabs_api notes ```
The rate of the absorption: the sum of the fluxes from the lumen into the intestinal
wall (the absorption of every segment and an apical influx). A readout of the definition,
an output of the intestine.

`Rabs_api = J_abs_du_api + J_abs_jej1_api + J_abs_jej2_api + J_abs_ile1_api + J_abs_ile2_api + J_abs_cae_api + J_abs_asc_api + J_abs_tra_api + J_abs_des_api + J_abs_sig_api + J_abs_rec_api`
```
  Reff_api notes ```
The rate of the efflux into the lumen: the sum of the fluxes from the intestinal
wall into the lumen (the apical efflux of every segment). A readout of the definition,
an output of the intestine.

`Reff_api = APISEC_du + APISEC_jej1 + APISEC_jej2 + APISEC_ile1 + APISEC_ile2`
```
  GU__APISEC_du notes ```
Process `APISEC` of the small intestine in the mucosa of the duodenum, its share `w_uniform_du` of
the capacity, on `fu_api / K_mu_api * Cmu_du_api`.
```
  GU__APISEC_jej1 notes ```
Process `APISEC` of the small intestine in the mucosa of the upper jejunum, its share `w_uniform_jej1`
of the capacity, on `fu_api / K_mu_api * Cmu_jej1_api`.
```
  GU__APISEC_jej2 notes ```
Process `APISEC` of the small intestine in the mucosa of the lower jejunum, its share `w_uniform_jej2`
of the capacity, on `fu_api / K_mu_api * Cmu_jej2_api`.
```
  GU__APISEC_ile1 notes ```
Process `APISEC` of the small intestine in the mucosa of the upper ileum, its share `w_uniform_ile1`
of the capacity, on `fu_api / K_mu_api * Cmu_ile1_api`.
```
  GU__APISEC_ile2 notes ```
Process `APISEC` of the small intestine in the mucosa of the lower ileum, its share `w_uniform_ile2`
of the capacity, on `fu_api / K_mu_api * Cmu_ile2_api`.
```
  Rfeces_api notes ```
The rate of the fecal excretion: the net flux of the intestine into the feces. A
readout of the definition, an output of the intestine.

`Rfeces_api = J_feces_du_api + J_feces_jej1_api + J_feces_jej2_api + J_feces_ile1_api + J_feces_ile2_api + J_feces_cae_api + J_feces_asc_api + J_feces_tra_api + J_feces_des_api + J_feces_sig_api + J_tr_rec_api + J_feces_rec_api + J_trs_rec_api`
```
  GU__Aabs_api notes ```
The amount absorbed from the lumen into the intestinal wall since the start, the
integral of the absorption (`J_abs_du_api + J_abs_jej1_api + J_abs_jej2_api + J_abs_ile1_api + J_abs_ile2_api + J_abs_cae_api + J_abs_asc_api + J_abs_tra_api + J_abs_des_api + J_abs_sig_api + J_abs_rec_api`). A state which nothing drains.

`dAabs_api/dt = J_abs_du_api + J_abs_jej1_api + J_abs_jej2_api + J_abs_ile1_api + J_abs_ile2_api + J_abs_cae_api + J_abs_asc_api + J_abs_tra_api + J_abs_des_api + J_abs_sig_api + J_abs_rec_api`
```
  GU__Aapp_api notes ```
The oral dose which the intestine has applied: the outflows of the dose states (the
dissolution and the emptying of a tablet, the application of a solution) since the
start. A state which nothing drains.

`dAapp_api/dt = -(-(J_po_api + J_trs_st_api) * Mr_api) / Mr_api + -(-J_sol_api * Mr_api) / Mr_api`
```
  Fa_api notes ```
The gross absorbed fraction of the oral dose: the amount absorbed from the lumen
over the oral dose given until then, 0 before a dose; before the first pass of the
wall and the liver (above the bioavailability), and with the absorption of what reaches
the lumen otherwise (the bile, an efflux), which can make it exceed 1. A readout
of the definition, an output of the intestine.

`Fa_api = piecewise(Aabs_api / (PODOSE_api / Mr_api + SOLDOSE_api / Mr_api + Aapp_api), (PODOSE_api / Mr_api + SOLDOSE_api / Mr_api + Aapp_api) > 0 mmole, 0 dimensionless)`
```
  Cout_sp_api notes ```
Plasma concentration of the blood leaving the organ.

`Cout_api = Cpl_api`
```
  SP__PS_api notes ```
Passive exchange between plasma and tissue: the share of the whole-body exchange
`ftissue` by the tissue volume of the organ relative to the reference tissue volume. ftissue
multiplies `fu*(Cpl - Cti/Kp)` (the unbound plasma concentration and the tissue concentration as plasma
equivalent), so its fitted values differ from those of the hand-written models, where
it multiplied the total concentrations.

`PS_api = ftissue_api * Vsp * (1 dimensionless - f_vas_sp) / Vti_total_ref_api`
```
  SP__Cu_ti_api notes ```
Unbound concentration of the tissue; an observer.

`Cu_ti_api = fu_api / Kp_api * Cti_api`
